-- title:
--   Eichler–Shimura: λ-adic representations of a weight-two eigenform
-- statement:
--   Let $N\ge 1$ and let $g$ be a cusp form of weight $2$ for $\Gamma_0(N)$ which is a normalized eigenform in the sense that its $q$-expansion coefficients $a_n=\mathrm{qCoeff}\,g\,n$ satisfy $a_1=1$, $a_{mn}=a_ma_n$ for coprime $m,n$, $a_{p^{r+2}}=a_pa_{p^{r+1}}-p\,a_{p^r}$ for primes $p\nmid N$, and $a_{p^{r+2}}=a_pa_{p^{r+1}}$ for primes $p\mid N$. Let $R_g=\mathbb{Z}[a_n:n\in\mathbb{N}]\subseteq\mathbb{C}$ be the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra generated by these coefficients and let $P\subset R_g$ be a maximal ideal. Then there are a prime $p$; a ring $O$ which is a characteristic-zero complete discrete valuation domain with finite residue field, complete for the $\mathfrak m_O$-adic topology; a ring homomorphism $\iota\colon R_g\to O$; and a $\mathfrak m_O$-adically continuous two-dimensional representation $\rho$ of $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$, that is, a finite free $O$-module $V$ with $\operatorname{rank}_O V=2$ together with a monoid homomorphism $\rho.\rho$ from the $\mathbb{Q}$-automorphisms of $\mathrm{AlgebraicClosure}\ \mathbb{Q}$ to $\mathrm{End}_O(V)$ such that for each $n$ there is a finite extension $L/\mathbb{Q}$ inside $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $\rho(\sigma)v-v\in\mathfrak m_O^n\cdot V$ for all $v\in V$ whenever $\sigma$ fixes $L$ pointwise; these satisfy: the image of $p$ lies in $P$, $p\in\mathfrak m_O$, $\iota$ is injective, $\iota^{-1}(\mathfrak m_O)=P$; for every prime $\ell\nmid N$ with $\ell\ne p$, every valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $\ell$ a nonunit of $A$ and every $\sigma$ lying in the decomposition subgroup of $A$ and acting on the residue field of $A$ by $x\mapsto x^{\ell}$, the characteristic polynomial of $\rho(\sigma)$ is $X^2-\iota(a_\ell)X+\ell$; and for every such $\ell$, $\rho(\sigma)=1$ for every $\sigma$ in the image of the inertia subgroup of every valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ having $\ell$ as a nonunit.
--
--   This is the Eichler–Shimura construction in weight two, in the form of the compatible family of $\lambda$-adic representations attached to a normalized eigenform, indexed intrinsically by the maximal ideals of the order generated by its Fourier coefficients, with the Frobenius characteristic polynomials $X^2-a_\ell X+\ell$ at primes of good reduction. It supplies the modular Galois representations used further on, and is invoked in the variant [`CuspForm.IsNormalizedEigenform.exists_galoisRepAdic_charpoly_frobenius_eq_of_ringHom_integralClosure`](thm.html#CuspForm.IsNormalizedEigenform.exists_galoisRepAdic_charpoly_frobenius_eq_of_ringHom_integralClosure), where the coefficient embedding is given in advance.
